          ],
          "returnType": "void",
          "description": "Defines how the application loads a class. decode receives the fetched data and returns the resource, synchronously or as a promise; fetching, caching, deduplication and ownership stay with the loader. read chooses whether decode gets bytes (the default), text, parsed JSON or a Blob. A document parser validates and migrates versioned documents before decode runs, and a codec takes full control of how the response is read. A loader factory replaces decode when the type needs per-application state; supply a separate instance for each application, which owns and destroys it. The type id names the type in caches and saved documents, so keep it stable across releases; it cannot be shared with another class. Define the same class and id again before its first request to replace its factory."
        },
